CONNECTION ROUND TRIP
1. Configured the synthetic endpoint and prepared Picture Control capability/
   slot reads. The synthetic NCP was imported with the actual file picker.
2. Explicitly confirmed empty C2 import. UI reported saved and readback checked.
3. Completed the result and returned to preset root: green connected badge.
4. Entered Album: automatic handoff enumerated photos, green connected badge,
   initially 24+ items; no user reconnect was required.
5. After photo-viewer checks, returned to preset detail and selected Wi-Fi import.
   Confirmation reported the same held session, C3 empty. Explicitly confirmed
   C3; result again reported saved and readback checked.
6. Returned to Album camera photos: photos and green connected badge remained.
7. HOME while camera-photo grid active retained a foreground connection service.
   Returning brought the same Activity/task forward, with photos and connected
   status. This was an ordinary brief HOME check, not a new Doze certification.
8. Settings displayed Z6II, Wi-Fi, connected. Explicitly tapped Disconnect.
   Settings and Album then displayed disconnected; service dump was empty.
   dumpsys power reported Wake Locks: size=0, historical camera-lock release
   at 04:31:16.682Z. The protocol ends in transport_closed/CLOSED, with no
   CloseSession command. See the separate raw protocol log and audit.

REMOTE PHOTO VIEWER
